          "text": "Not quite -- `^4.17.21` allows any `4.x.x` at or above `4.17.21` (anything that doesn't bump the major version), so a fresh install could still pull `4.17.25` or similar. To actually pin it exactly, drop the caret and write `\"lodash\": \"4.17.21\"`, or just rely on the committed lockfile for reproducible installs."
