          "id": "prt_06b",
          "sessionID": "ses_24",
          "messageID": "msg_06",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Actually the opposite assumption applies here -- under semver, a major version bump (4 -> 5) is exactly the signal that breaking changes are allowed, not a guarantee of compatibility. Minor and patch bumps are the ones meant to stay backward compatible; major bumps are where APIs can change or get removed. I'd read the v5 migration guide/changelog first and do the upgrade as its own PR with the full test suite run, rather than folding it into today's work."
        },
        {
          "id": "prt_06c",
          "sessionID": "ses_24",
          "messageID": "msg_06",
